Title: The Price of Freedom
Credit: Scene 10 — revision draft A
Author: Art department draft, for Grace Taylor
Source:
	The Sabacc game, rewritten as a showcase for the mercenary cast.
	Every performer at this table has a moment. Baylan and Jasu are absent.
Draft date: 2026-08-01
Contact: gracetaylorwriter@hotmail.com


INT. MERCENARY SHIP - MAIN HOLD - NIGHT #10#

A work lamp hooked over a supply crate. Bulkhead fixtures
throw dirty light down the walls. Eight mercenaries crammed
into a hold built for cargo, perched on ammunition boxes, a
fuel drum, the deck itself.

YASLO BIS deals. He has the hands of a man who has done this
in worse rooms than this one.

MERC 1 - a Wookiee, greying at the muzzle - is folded into a
space that does not fit him, knees near his ears. A row of
thermal detonators sits across his chest rig, at eye level
for everybody sitting down.

MERC 2 is not playing. He works a whetstone along a blade,
glancing up now and then. The rifle across his knees has
small notches cut into the stock. A lot of them.

NYX
No, no, you have got that absolutely
wrong.

SHADA
We were all there, Nyx. We saw it.

They talk over each other. Nyx protests to the room, to the
ceiling, to anyone. MERC 3 leans back, and something new
swings off his chest rig - a cracked visor lens on a cord.

SHADA (cont'd)
(nodding at it)
That new?

MERC 3 turns it over with a finger. Says nothing. Grins.

SHADA (cont'd)
Charming.

A shape in the doorway. Full armour, blaster rifle in both
hands, still wet from outside.

NYX
Reya. Tell them what actually
happened on that job back on Naboo.

The mercenary takes off her helmet. REYA FENN's hair comes
down over the shoulders of the armour. She looks at the
room - the cards, the crate, the eight of them - like
someone remembering this is where she lives.

REYA FENN
I have walked my entire patrol.
Twice. In the wet.

She sets the helmet on a crate and leans the rifle beside
it.

REYA FENN (cont'd)
And you are still arguing about
Naboo.

The room enjoys this. Yaslo does not look up from the deal.

YASLO BIS
Am I dealing you in?

REYA FENN
You are.

She drops onto a crate and elbows the Wookiee
companionably. It is like elbowing a wall. He rumbles.

NYX
Well? Are you going to stand up for
me here?

Reya picks up her cards. Fans them. Looks at Nyx over the
top.

REYA FENN
You fell on top of him.

NYX
I jumped. To take him down. There is
a considerable difference.

Yaslo sets the deck down. Only then does he speak, without
heat, the way a man states a fact.

YASLO BIS
I was on the roof. Clear line on the
whole courtyard.

NYX
Yaslo-

YASLO BIS
You were facing the wrong way. You
went over a low wall you did not know
was there, and he broke your fall.

The hold goes up. MERC 1 slaps the crate and it jumps. MERC
3 is wheezing. MERC 2 does not look up from the whetstone,
but he is smiling.

MERC 4 laughs a half-beat after everyone else. He is the
youngest here by some way, and he checks the others before
he commits to it.

Nyx drops his head into his hands in mock ruin. Shada slings
an arm round his shoulders and knuckles his hair.

SHADA
Leave him alone. Can't be upsetting
Jasu's golden boy.

Nyx shoves her off. Shada goes with it easily - and on the
way back she plucks the top card off his hand, glances at
it, and lays it face down in front of him again, still
smiling.

Nyx has not noticed. Reya has.

NYX
Oh, can it. We all know Bay's her
right hand.

A murmur round the crate. Not a compliment, not an insult.
Just true, and they are all a little tired of it.

MERC 4
(to Reya, quietly)
Where is he tonight?

REYA FENN
(not looking up)
Where he always is. Somewhere else.

MERC 4 nods as though that means something, and folds. He
has good cards. He folds anyway.

Nyx raises an eyebrow at his own hand and the grin comes
back like nothing happened.

NYX
Right. This golden boy is about to
take every credit in this room.

He lays his hand down with a flourish. It is a good hand.

Beside him, without any ceremony whatsoever, MERC 1 turns
over an Idiot's Array.

The noise eight people make is the loudest thing in the film
so far. MERC 3 is on his feet. Reya has her head back. Yaslo
is already gathering the deck, entirely unsurprised, because
he dealt it.

MERC 1 sweeps the pot toward his chest with one enormous
forearm. His grenades sit in a row, inches from the pile.
Nobody looks at them. They have been there for years.

Nyx stares at the array, then at the ceiling.

NYX (cont'd)
Deal again.

YASLO BIS
Dealing.

The laughter settles to the low, easy noise of people who
have done this a thousand nights. Somebody slaps somebody's
back. Cards go round.

Only MERC 4 is quiet. He watches the others enjoy
themselves, and almost gets there.

CUT TO:
